task: form-recursive-depth-safety
agent: opus-depth
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/form-recursive-depth-safety
worktree: ../okay-wt-form-depth
spec: encode-side-depth-safety's own follow-up (found while auditing
  its own grep results a second time, at the operator's direct
  question "did you fix everything")

why: `okay-ui/Form.scala` has the SAME defect shape the codec arc
  closed twice already (decode side, then write side): `editAt`,
  `render`/`field`/`sumUi`/`listUi`, and `errorsOf`/`listErrors` all
  recurse on a Schema+Json pair's own depth, not a fixed schema shape
  — for a RECURSIVE schema (a Tree-like form field), depth is however
  deep the ACTUAL VALUE is. Three separate ways that value gets deep
  without any cap: (1) `editAt` recurses once per PATH SEGMENT, and a
  path is a dotted STRING an event carries — `Event.Submitted(_,
  edits)`'s own doc comment says a client folds edits locally and this
  folds "the SAME edit a live edit takes", i.e. a remote submission
  path exists; (2) a batch of many edits each adding one level to a
  recursive field (many `Choose`/`Add` events, one `Submitted`)
  accumulates an arbitrarily deep VALUE with no check anywhere; (3)
  `Form.of`/`Form.ofWith` take an arbitrary `Json` directly, not only
  one built through local edits.

what: `editAt`, the render pipeline (`render`/`field`/`sumUi`/
  `listUi`), and the validation pipeline (`errorsOf`/`listErrors`) get
  the same `Codecs.NativeThreshold`-then-`Cont.defer` split the codec
  arc already carries twice over (decode, then encode). `isList`/
  `isComposite`/`itemSchema`/`empty`/`leaf`/`leafEmpty` are schema-only
  dispatchers with no depth recursion — untouched.

predict: three separate mutually-recursive pipelines, not one — more
  surface than either codec lane, so likely to take longer. Genuinely
  unclear whether this UI layer is ever reachable by adversarial input
  at internet scale (unlike the codec's raw wire bytes) — worth
  stating plainly in the landing note rather than assuming either way.
  Needs new tests building a deep value/path directly (not through the
  real edit flow, to keep the test independent of edit's own
  correctness) and rendering/validating/editing it without overflow.
